{"name":"Carmen","hex":"#7c383f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Carmen","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Spanish .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A town in Oklahoma."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A male given name from Italian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Carmen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Carmen","blocks":[{"text":"Carmen is an opera in four acts by the French composer Georges Bizet. The libretto was written by Henri Meilhac and Ludovic Halévy, based on the novella of the same title by Prosper Mérimée. The opera was first performed by the Opéra-Comique in Paris on 3 March 1875, where its breaking of conventions shocked and scandalised its first audiences. Bizet died suddenly after the 33rd performance, unaware that the work would achieve international acclaim within the following ten years. Carmen has since become one of the most popular and frequently performed operas in the classical canon; the \"Habanera\" and \"Seguidilla\" from act 1 and the \"Toreador Song\" from act 2 are among the best known of all operatic arias."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Prudent-Louis_Leray_-_Poster_for_the_premi%C3%A8re_of_Georges_Bizet%27s_Carmen.jpg/330px-Prudent-Louis_Leray_-_Poster_for_the_premi%C3%A8re_of_Georges_Bizet%27s_Carmen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmen","wikidata":"Q185968"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Merimee_sketch_001.png/500px-Merimee_sketch_001.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Merimee_sketch_001.png/500px-Merimee_sketch_001.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Prosper Mérimée, whose novella Carmen (1845) inspired the opera","link